    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML aims to fully automate the machine learning process end-to-end, democratizing Machine Learning to non-experts</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML targets at addressing complex design choices and high human labor cost in classical machine learning.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML aims to fully automate the machine learning process end-to-end</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML systems can be categorized, these are summarized as follows</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML systems can be categorized, these are summarized as follows: level. Search of estimators/predictors . This level refers to the task of dening / determining a function mapping inputs to outputs</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML research has focused on combining two tasks: machine learning pipeline building and intelligent model hyperparameter search.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Designing a good AutoML system requires careful consideration of all these three factors, which set up three core issues of AutoML: how to design a good search space? how to desi</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">empirical success when compared to other AutoML systems. However, by stacking models on top of each other, our search space is much larger than that of single-model AutoML systems such as TPOT or AutoSklearn.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SmartML</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">automl-streams, the experimental framework proposed in this work</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">most comparisons of AutoML systems focus on quantitative criteria such as</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">are also used in the AutoML system H YPEROPT SKLEARN</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML system H YPEROPT SKLEARN</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
