    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">uses Bayesian Optimization (Sequential model-based optimization) to search for optimal hyperparameter settings of the pipeline.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">hyperparameter_scale_min_max_learning_parameters_initial_learning_rate_log_5_10_5_5_conv1_l_2_penalty</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">warmstarting optimization by meta-learning has already been successfully applied before [ 4 , 5 , 6 ], but never to an optimization problem as complex as that of searching the space of instantiations of a full-edged ML framework.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">search this space to optimize 10-fold cross-validation performance</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">hyperparameter optimization as an algorithmic approach for nding optimal values of architecture independent hyperparameters</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Bayesian optimization (BO) is a model-based approach for gradient-free black-box function optimization, such as hyperparameter optimization.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Bayesian optimization (BO) is a successful methodology to optimize black-box functions that are expensive to evaluate.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">selecting the best-performing hyperparameter combination.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">techniques for the automatic optimization of hyper-parameters</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">grid search is the most commonly-used form of hyperparameter optimization</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Gradient-based algorithms are not a prevalent choice for hyper-parameter optimization</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">hyperparameters are values that control the model conguration or the training setup and thus need to be set before training the model.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
