    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML targets at addressing complex design choices and high human labor cost in classical machine learning. Through the process of atomization of learning configurations</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Automated Machine Learning (AutoML) is a rapidly rising subfield of Machine Learning. AutoML aims to fully automate the machine learning process end-to-end</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">when talking about AutoML throughout the paper it means solving the combined algorithm selection and hyperparameter optimization problem, or CASH for short</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML research has focused on combining two tasks: machine learning pipeline building and intelligent model hyperparameter search.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML throughout the paper it means solving the combined algorithm selection and hyperparameter optimization problem, or CASH for short</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML aims to fully automate the machine learning process end-to-end, democratizing Machine Learning to non-experts</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML aims to fully automate the machine learning process end-to-end, democratizing Machine Learning to non-experts and drastically increasing the productivity of expert analysts.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">systems for automating DNN configuration have been developed, such as Google AutoML</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AutoML targets at addressing complex design choices and high human labor cost in classical machine learning.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">our search space is much larger than that of single-model AutoML systems such as TPOT or AutoSklearn.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">attempts to atomize (all or a part of) learning configurations and then recombine them through optimizing performance measure</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">current AutoML solutions generate vast and rich information that can be useful for a number of purposes.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
