    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Neural architecture search (NAS) has been successfully applied to design model architectures for image classication and language models</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">automatic model design. In ENAS, a controller discovers neural network architectures by searching for an optimal subgraph</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Neural Architecture Search can design good models from scratch</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">only the NAS search process with AutoKeras but also utilize resource adaptability and result tracking with Auptimizer</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Efcient Neural Architecture Search (ENAS), a fast and inexpensive approach for automatic model design.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Neural architecture search (NAS) has been successfully applied to design model architectures</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ENAS takes 11 . 5 hours to discover the convolution cell and the reduction cell</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the most typical application is neural architecture search, as the neural architectures can usually be represented as a DAG</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
