    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HP: These include all hyperparameters used for training the neural networks, e.g. initial learning rate and learning rate decay</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">hyper-parameters are classied as continuous, discrete, and categorical hyper-parameters.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">rank hyperparameters x j on each problem D i by the validation error R A ( D i , x j )</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Different hyperparameters are not independent. Instead, their values are intertwined.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">possibly having to explore its hyper-parameters</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">We propose therefore to rank hyperparameters x j on each problem D i by the validation error R A ( D i , x j )</hasEvidenceText>
